findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase distinguished NotFound from other errors in from_file_or_default.
    Reviewer verified config precedence chain but didn't flag the unwrap_or_default
    swallowing all error types. Config loading tests exist but none test parse-error
    vs not-found distinction.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer marked '[VERIFIED] Error message security (CWE-209) \u2014 error.rs:8-44:\
    \ Error Display implementations are concise and don't leak internal paths, stack\
    \ traces, or permission details.' TEA also wrote security tests for CWE-209. However,\
    \ the finding is about stderr via eprintln leaking Display impl details, and the\
    \ reviewer noted the Display impls are concise \u2014 partial catch at best. The\
    \ core issue of needing a user_message() sanitization layer was not flagged."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection CRLF tests in siem_client.rs and security.rs.\
    \ Dev implemented CRLF sanitization in client.rs:39-42,47-51. However, the deeper\
    \ issue \u2014 using raw String instead of validated TenantId from axiathon-core\
    \ \u2014 was not flagged by any phase."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: ''six dependencies are pinned directly in
    the crate Cargo.toml with hardcoded versions... The root Cargo.toml [workspace.dependencies]
    section is untouched. This violates the workspace dependency management architecture.'''
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'Reviewer noted the test for unknown keys is vacuous (config_rejects_unknown_keys_gracefully
    discards result) but did not flag the actual production issue: serde silently
    ignoring unknown fields like token, leaving secrets on disk. The reviewer asked
    for the test to be fixed but missed the underlying design flaw of not using deny_unknown_fields.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM] Vacuous test: client_config_handles_unreadable_file\
    \ \u2014 'is_ok() || is_err() is a tautology \u2014 always true. This tests nothing.'"
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM] Vacuous test: client_config_rejects_unknown_keys_gracefully\
    \ \u2014 'The result is discarded without assertion. The test verifies doesn't\
    \ panic but doesn't verify what happened.'"
